00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:09.106
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:09.406 --> 00:02:11.592
Rithy, what game do you like?

46
00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.814
I like football. I play with my team.

47
00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:18.559
Do you always win?

48
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.930
No! Sometimes we win, but sometimes we lose.

49
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:27.112
How do you feel when you lose?

50
00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:31.032
A little sad, but we always play fair.

51
00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:34.757
Grammar focus: Sometimes  but .

52
00:02:35.057 --> 00:02:38.113
Sometimes we win, but sometimes we lose.

53
00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:42.108
Use 'but' to join two different ideas in one sentence.

54
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:45.665
Now read and listen. Game Time.

55
00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.359
I love playing games with my team.

56
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.345
Sometimes we win, and sometimes we lose.

57
00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.031
